{{Quote|Hey kid! A storm's comin' soon. You better get inside.|Glem warns Kazuda Xiono of a storm|<ref name="Triple Dark" />}}
'''Glem''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Rodian]] who worked at the [[Colossus loading docks|loading docks]] on the ''[[Colossus]]'' refueling station on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Castilon]] during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]]. During a [[triple dark]] storm, he warned [[Kazuda Xiono]] of a possible [[Attack on the Colossus|pirate attack]]. Later, [[Teroj Kee]] locked Xiono in a crate and told Glem to dispose of it. Glem did so, and found an escaped Xiono clutching on a magnetic crane. During the [[First Order]]'s occupation of the ''Colossus'', Glem was confronted by [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] about his identification.

==Biography==
===Kaz arrives===
{{Quote|Triple dark. That's the second time I've heard that today. What does that mean.''"<br />"''It's a type of storm, low visibility. Sometimes pirates use them for cover to attack the station.|Kazuda Xiono asks Glem about a triple dark|<ref name="Triple Dark" />}}
[[File:AuntZsTavern-Databank.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Glem (second left) was involved in a bar fight]]
By the year [[34 ABY]], Glem was working on the ''[[Colossus]]'', a refueling station on the [[ocean]] [[planet]] [[Castilon]], at its [[Colossus loading docks|loading docks]].<ref name="Glem DB" /> During that year, [[Kazuda Xiono]], a newly recruited [[Resistance]] [[spy]], arrived there to work at [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station]], while secretly spying on the place. During his first visit to [[Aunt Z's Tavern]], he was involved in a dispute with the [[Klatooinian]] [[Bolza Grool]]. When Grool hit a [[service droid]], a cup flew from it and hit Glem, who was sitting at one of the nearby tables. Glem threw his cups back, and they hit the [[Snivvian]] [[Nod]]. As an all-out bar fight ensued, Nod attacked Glem, and had managed to put him into a headlock by the time [[Jarek Yeager]] broke up the fight. Following the fight, the [[Nikto]] [[Neeku Vozo]] entered Xiono into the race that took place the following [[Standard day|day]]. Glem joined in on the betting after [[Torra Doza]] was revealed as the opposing racer.<ref name="Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref>

Sometime after, Glem was in the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]] when Xiono was spying on other residents. Later, Glem found him at the loading docks, looking at his [[Kaz's lucky trophy|lucky trophy]]. He recommended going inside as a [[triple dark]] storm had arrived. Xiono wasn't bothered about the storm, so Glem told him about how the [[Warbird gang]], a band of [[pirate]]s, used it to attack the ''Colossus'', further pointing out their leader [[Kragan Gorr]] when the boy brought his name up. Glem then left Xiono to process the information for himself. As he had predicted, the Warbird gang did [[Attack on the Colossus|attack]], but were thwarted soon enough.<ref name="Triple Dark" />

At one point, Glem was walking through the hallways of the ''Colossus'' when Xiono shoved past him, causing the Rodian to yell back.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire">{{Resistance|Fuel for the Fire}}</ref> Soon after, he was at Aunt Z's Tavern. There, he discussed the [[bounty]] on two fugitive children with the [[Gotal]] [[Yani]]. Glem predicted the pair would be on the other side of [[the galaxy]] by that time and asked [[Z'Vk'Thkrkza|Aunt Z]] for another [[Jet juice]]. He was later at the marketplace talking to [[Vic (Colossus)|Vic]] when two [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] of the [[First Order]] came to investigate sightings of the children.<ref name="Children from Tehar">{{Resistance|The Children from Tehar}}</ref>

===Troubles at work===
{{Quote|Hey! What are you doing up there?''"<br />"''Well&hellip;what are you doing down there.''"<br />"''What! I'm working!|Glem discovers Xiono clinging to a crane|<ref name="Dangerous Business">{{Resistance|Dangerous Business}}</ref>}}
Glem was driving a [[repulsorlift]] through the loading docks when [[Synara San]], a newer employee, got into a fight with the dock worker [[Orthog]]. Later that day, the Warbird gang [[Raid on the Colossus|attacked]] the ''Colossus'' again. As some of them began raiding the loading docks, Glem hid behind a crate. He soon left his cover and the pirate attack eventually finished with the reactivation of the ''Colossus''{{'}} [[turbolaser]]s.<ref name="Synara's Score">{{Resistance|Synara's Score}}</ref> Glem was at Aunt Z's tavern when two members of the [[Guavian Death Gang]] confronted the racer [[Marcus Speedstar]]. Following the commotion, Jarek Yeager arrived and challenged Speedstar to the [[Platform Classic]]. Speedstar accepted, and Aunt Z began the betting, causing Glem to cheer as it began. He later watched the race with the other patrons of the bar. After Speedstar won, Glem returned to the tavern and talked to [[Al]] when Speedstar paid his winnings to the Guavian Death Gang.<ref name="Platform Classic">{{Resistance|The Platform Classic}}</ref>

A while later, Glem passed Torra Doza and Xiono when they visited the marketplace one day.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms">{{Resistance|Secrets and Holograms}}</ref> He was working at the loading docks when Xiono and Ryvora found a baby [[Rokkna]] while receiving some salvaged parts. Glem was later at a landing pad when Neeku was searching for the infant creature.<ref name="Bibo">{{Resistance|Bibo (episode)}}</ref> One day, Glem was at the loading docks when the [[Keteerian]] [[Teroj Kee]] asked him to dispose of a crate in [[dock 23]]. While listening to music, he had it dropped into the ocean, not knowing that Kee had trapped Xiono inside of it. After the crate was dropped, Glem found Xiono clinging onto the magnetic crane and asked why he was up there. Xiono made up silly excuses, so the Rodian left.<ref name="Dangerous Business" />

===Under the occupation===
{{Quote|You! Show us your identification.''"<br />"''Oh&hellip;right, yes. I, I have it&hellip;I&hellip;uh&hellip;wait just a minute.''"<br />"''We don't have all day.|A [[Unidentified First Order stormtrooper commander|stormtrooper]] demands Glem's identification|<ref name="First Order Occupation">{{Resistance|The First Order Occupation}}</ref>}}
During the First Order's [[Occupation of the Colossus|occupation of the ''Colossus'']], Glem was confronted by three of their stormtroopers in the marketplace, asking for his identification. When he was unable to find it, the [[trooper]]s tried to arrest him. Xiono intervened, and Glem then found his I.D. in time, and the stormtroopers let him go. Later, he was at the loading docks, convincing Synara to work the night-shift. She let agreed, but told him to prepare the containers ahead of [[time]] in exchange. As she left, two stormtroopers arrived in search of her, suspecting her to be a spy for the Warbird gang. Glem was still at the loading docks when she returned, and two stormtroopers searched around for her. They questioned him on where Synara was, and he directed them in her direction.<ref name="First Order Occupation" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Have you seen this person?''"<br />"''Yeah, that's Synara San. She just over there.|A stormtrooper questions Glem|<ref name="First Order Occupation" />}}
Glem was a male Rodian with [[Color|black]] [[eye]]s, green skin, and a bulky figure.<ref name="Triple Dark" /> He had a gravel voice and liked to gamble for better shifts at his job at the ''Colossus'' loading docks. He showed no loyalty to the new employee Synara San and pointed the First Order in her direction when asked of it.<ref name="Glem DB" />

==Equipment==
Glem wore [[Color|gray]] tunic with dark gray sleeves and trousers.<ref name="Recruit" /> When working at the loading docks, he wore a yellow vest and sandy brown colored undershirt and trousers.<ref name="Triple Dark" />

==Behind the scenes==
Glem first appeared in the first episode of ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|Season One]], "[[The Recruit]],"<ref name="Recruit" /> on [[October 7]] [[2018]].<ref name="Resistance trailer">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-resistance-trailer|text=''Star Wars Resistance'' Trailer Revealed}}</ref> He was voiced by [[Dee Bradley Baker]],<ref name="Recruit" /> who also voiced the [[clone trooper]]s in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' and ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="Star Wars voice actors">{{SW|url=news/8-star-wars-voice-actors-who-play-multiple-animated-characters|text=8 ''Star Wars'' Voice Actors Who Played Multiple Characters|nolive=1}}</ref>

